WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:03.480
<b>Cocktail Corn</b>

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:06.460
Welcome.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:08.950
Welcome.

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:11.990
So cute!

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:13.790
Ahem.

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:16.430
Tazuna-kun, a little louder.

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:18.250
And a little more expressive.

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:18.920
Got it?

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:19.990
Okay!

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:23.980
I think it works for 
Koyori-chan though, right?

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:37.700
Why are you taking a photo?

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:41.240
Because you're cute!

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:43.520
Oh, by "you" I mean Koyori-chan, okay?

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:44.990
Right...

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:46.920
No, wait!

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.520
Now I'll take one more with this.

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:51.520
I said...

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:35.630
I never thought Koyori-kun 
would change so much.

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:37.180
In such a short time, too...

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:40.950
I'm glad it was you, Tazuna-kun.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:44.510
I'm really glad it was you!

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:48.520
Scary.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:56.280
She's scared of me!

00:02:56.280 --> 00:03:00.650
But if you want to think positive, that means
she's changed enough to be scared now.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:03.440
I want to scare her more.

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:05.280
No, that's not a good idea.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:06.290
I understand.

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:09.140
Koyori, it's okay.

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:13.290
Makihara-sensei seems to realize 
that something's wrong with him.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:17.370
And Tazuna-kun, you're getting 
more brutal towards me every day.

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:19.300
But that aside...

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:22.860
I am grateful to you.

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:27.310
If Koyori-kun had never woken up, 
I wouldn't have been able to see her like this.

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:30.330
She's helped me.

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:32.710
Tazuna always protects me.

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:38.820
But... I see...

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:42.430
If she can speak, that means...

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:44.820
And then that castle in the Ziggurat...

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.330
<b>Chizuru-san</b>

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:48.720
Her language abilities 
themselves weren't lost.

00:03:46.070 --> 00:03:47.330
Chizuru-san?

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:49.580
Yes?

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:50.200
Her memories...

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:51.330
<i>Hello? Tazuna-kun?</i>

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:51.330
Hey, um, are you listening?

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:53.580
I'll make this quick.

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:56.520
How do you and Koyori-chan 
feel about a part-time job?

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:57.840
You can try it first.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:05.960
Okay, Koyori-chan, you can 
serve customers in the front.

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:08.960
If there's something you don't 
understand, don't hesitate to ask.

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:10.850
Tazuna-kun, you man the kitchen.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:12.380
Okay.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:17.880
Chizuru-san, that's impossible.

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:20.520
I can let go of her hand for a while, but...

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:21.860
That's right...

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:25.360
So both of you can man the kitchen.

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:30.280
I'm satisfied that I got to see 
Koyori-chan in her uniform.

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:37.020
Manager, stop staring at 
Koyori-chan and work, please!

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:39.980
They're talking to you, Manager Hayate!

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:41.130
Huh? Me?

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:44.350
No, they were talking to you, Senpai.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.650
Oh, hi, Tazuna-kun.

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:48.640
You look good, Koyori-chan.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:52.080
Why do they actually call me 
manager at times like this?

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:53.440
The shop's gonna blow up...

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:56.150
That would be bad, so I'll work!

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:59.310
Okay, let's work, too.

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:00.150
Yeah.

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:05.080
Takatsuki-kun, warm up the hamburg steaks.

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:07.160
The fries will be ready soon.

00:05:07.730 --> 00:05:08.660
Okay!

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:18.890
Okay.

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:30.480
You guys make a great combination.

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:33.560
There's two of us,
 so the overall efficiency is low.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:36.060
You've only been working for two hours.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:38.820
It's kind of depressing to see 
how fast you're picking stuff up.

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:43.320
Koyori's used to it, that's all.

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:45.070
Tazuna helps me.

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:47.070
Well...

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:52.520
But why did Chizuru-san ask 
us to try out this job?

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:55.580
Since the two of us can only work together,

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:57.660
we just get in the way.

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:58.650
Excuse me.

00:05:58.650 --> 00:05:59.450
Right.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:01.960
No...

00:06:02.390 --> 00:06:06.780
If you were just holding hands for 
no reason you'd only get in the way,

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:08.840
but you're a little different.

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:14.490
And if Senpai thought you were 
only going to get in the way,

00:06:14.490 --> 00:06:16.350
she wouldn't talk to you.

00:06:18.530 --> 00:06:20.850
She saw how you moved at the school festival.

00:06:21.330 --> 00:06:24.400
She said nobody else could 
move as a pair like you do.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:26.400
She was really impressed.

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:31.200
And Koyori-chan's an even 
better cook now, right?

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:34.280
It's been a while since we saw you,
 and now you can talk...

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:37.380
Both of us were surprised.

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:40.870
I don't know what Senpai's thinking,

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:45.200
but I think this is a good 
chance for the two of you.

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:47.070
For us?

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:47.880
That's right.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:51.560
If you do some work when you're a student, 
even if it's just a part-time job,

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:53.870
it'll be useful when you grow up.

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:56.140
Even if you don't work in the same business.

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:58.640
You mean it's just for the experience?

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:00.600
That's part of it,

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:04.230
but the other part is that you understand 
how people feel when they work.

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:09.950
Well, it's like how Hand Shakers don't 
understand each other until they fight.

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:11.420
Something like that.

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:16.030
Well, in the future, when you finally 
let go of each other's hands,

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:18.280
I bet it will be useful.

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:21.040
When we let go of each other's hands...

00:07:21.730 --> 00:07:23.320
Makihara-san's working on a way

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:27.660
to deal with Koyori-chan's problems, right?

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:32.050
Someday it will work out.

00:07:32.740 --> 00:07:34.260
Someday, huh?

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:39.560
Takatsuki-kun, can you wash the dishes?

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:41.450
Sure.

00:07:44.890 --> 00:07:48.440
There's more to life than 
Hand Shaker battles.

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:52.040
We lost, but our lives are still going on.

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:55.940
Well, I understand what 
it is you're carrying...

00:07:56.530 --> 00:07:59.580
It's a little too heavy. I'm sorry.

00:08:00.230 --> 00:08:02.680
But we took your wish...

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:04.080
That's okay.

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:06.360
It's frustrating and disappointing,

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:07.960
but Senpai's in a good mood.

00:08:08.260 --> 00:08:09.530
Is she?

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:10.210
Is that order correct?

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:12.460
Don't tell her this,

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:14.720
but she used to be more tense before.

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:16.720
Welcome!

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:20.740
I actually wanted to thank you.

00:08:21.670 --> 00:08:24.230
She changed after she fought you.

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:28.600
She's really lively when she works,

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:31.240
and when she gets mad at me, too.

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:38.260
If nothing else, all the 
employees here love her.

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:39.740
What?

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:41.850
Were you complaining about me behind my back?

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:44.430
Senpai, no...

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:45.750
It was... um...

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:47.850
Did you think I wouldn't notice?

00:08:47.850 --> 00:08:49.000
I was wondering what you were up to!

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:51.720
Were you complaining about me?

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:54.300
Any whining counts as complaining, right?

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:56.250
That's not fair.

00:08:56.250 --> 00:08:57.710
So, Tazuna-kun,

00:08:57.710 --> 00:08:59.260
what did Hayate say?

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:01.350
Um...

00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:03.690
He loves you.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:12.030
Hayate?

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:14.430
Why are you being so stupid?!

00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:18.000
Explode... I'm gonna explode!

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:19.100
That's not true!

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:22.920
I didn't say I like you.

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:25.680
But it's not that I don't like you...

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:26.710
It's not!

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:29.630
You're not in elementary school!

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:32.710
Wait, who are you saying 
is in elementary school?

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:34.360
I did not say that!

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:37.220
I'm sorry for thinking you look 
like a middle-school student.

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:39.450
Even if you're apologizing, 
that's still complaining.

00:09:39.450 --> 00:09:40.780
Nothing I say is okay.

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:42.360
That's mean.

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:43.600
Oh, jeez!

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:45.730
Oh, Tazuna-kun, Koyori-chan,

00:09:46.490 --> 00:09:48.230
your friends are here.

00:09:48.740 --> 00:09:49.800
Friends?

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:51.730
I'll give you a break to go see them.

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:53.730
What about me?

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:55.900
You do their work as well.

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:57.240
Get going!

00:09:57.240 --> 00:09:59.840
This is an abuse of power!

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:00.900
Does she like him?

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:03.400
Let's go.

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:08.840
Koyori-chan! Tazuna-kun!

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:27.140
Sorry, we came to see you.

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:30.150
How did you know we're working here?

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:33.900
Koyori-chan told me.

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:38.110
When did you send that photo?

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:40.660
Chizuru said to send it 
to an important friend.

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:45.350
An important friend...

00:10:46.920 --> 00:10:49.160
I'm considered one, too.

00:10:50.930 --> 00:10:53.170
It looks good on you, Koyori-chan.

00:10:55.810 --> 00:10:58.720
Sorry my sis came barging in.

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:01.180
No, it's fine.

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:06.430
She's always like this...

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:08.150
But please take care of her.

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:11.690
I do a good job of being student 
council president at school!

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:14.570
I'm sure, but...

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:17.310
At your core, Sis, you're...

00:11:17.310 --> 00:11:19.630
He trailed off.

00:11:19.630 --> 00:11:21.520
She does take care of us, yes.

00:11:21.520 --> 00:11:23.200
That's my Tazuna-kun!

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:26.700
Don't spoil her too much.

00:11:27.760 --> 00:11:29.990
Masaru is so mean.

00:11:29.990 --> 00:11:31.210
Masaru...

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:33.660
I'd heard about it,

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:35.900
but I guess you really can speak.

00:11:35.900 --> 00:11:36.830
Yeah.

00:11:36.830 --> 00:11:39.580
I want to play Precious Memories 
with both you and Tazuna.

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:40.920
Me, too?

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:43.220
Precious Memories? That card game?

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:46.220
It's fun.

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:49.470
Sure, it's a good game, but...

00:11:49.470 --> 00:11:51.980
Can you teach me, too?

00:11:52.710 --> 00:11:54.660
Teach you?

00:11:55.970 --> 00:11:58.940
Masaru is good at teaching, too!

00:11:58.940 --> 00:12:00.990
He taught me.

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:05.360
Masaru kept asking me to play,

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:07.180
and I didn't have a choice.

00:12:07.180 --> 00:12:09.490
You're the one who said you wanted to do it.

00:12:11.090 --> 00:12:13.370
But it's good.

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:14.500
Yeah, but...

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:17.630
He really is good at teaching.

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:20.510
He is the Demon Emperor of the End!

00:12:20.830 --> 00:12:23.650
The Dead End Emperor!

00:12:23.650 --> 00:12:24.510
Sis!

00:12:24.790 --> 00:12:27.000
Dead End Emperor?

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:28.510
Emperor...

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:30.060
Emperor?

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:31.840
Huh. Emperor.

00:12:31.840 --> 00:12:33.530
The Demon Emperor of the End...

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:35.130
That's right.

00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:37.560
My little brother is the Dead End Emperor!

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:38.520
Sis...

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:40.830
Dead End Emperor.

00:12:40.830 --> 00:12:42.760
Can you teach me sometime?

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:47.660
This is your dead end!

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:52.160
Your drinks are here, Emperor-sama.

00:12:53.590 --> 00:12:55.670
That's not what you were talking about?

00:12:58.980 --> 00:13:00.880
Break time's over.

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:03.150
Let's go back.

00:13:03.150 --> 00:13:04.380
Just a little...

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:07.610
Go without me for just a little while.

00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:10.390
Okay.

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:11.780
Catch up soon, okay?

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:13.530
Bye.

00:13:17.210 --> 00:13:18.900
Thanks for your message.

00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:24.400
I hope I was able to help.

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:25.680
Yeah.

00:13:25.680 --> 00:13:27.050
We're together.

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:36.920
I want to be like Koyori-chan 
and Tazuna-kun, don't you?

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:40.970
You and I are different, right, Sis?

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:49.930
Good work. This isn't much, but...

00:13:53.010 --> 00:13:54.510
Thank you.

00:13:54.510 --> 00:13:56.940
The other employees loved you.

00:13:57.290 --> 00:14:01.930
Some people were bothered by the fact 
 you had to be together to work,

00:14:01.930 --> 00:14:05.050
but they're willing to accept it now.

00:14:05.050 --> 00:14:08.990
The two of you go three times 
as fast as other people.

00:14:08.990 --> 00:14:11.310
They were being mean to me.

00:14:11.310 --> 00:14:13.890
"Are you still failing?"

00:14:13.890 --> 00:14:15.950
Don't let it get you down.

00:14:16.630 --> 00:14:20.490
I'd like to officially hire you.

00:14:20.490 --> 00:14:22.460
Think about it, okay?

00:14:24.070 --> 00:14:26.330
Yes. Thank you very much.

00:14:26.330 --> 00:14:27.220
Thank you.

00:14:27.220 --> 00:14:29.150
It's nothing.

00:14:29.150 --> 00:14:31.920
Anyway, you worked hard for that money,

00:14:31.920 --> 00:14:33.220
so why not go on a date?

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:35.540
A date?

00:14:36.280 --> 00:14:37.320
A date?

00:14:37.730 --> 00:14:39.730
A date?

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:41.730
Yes, a date.

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:44.540
Wait, you don't have to get red!

00:14:44.540 --> 00:14:46.620
You're a grown man!

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:49.230
I couldn't help it.

00:14:49.230 --> 00:14:51.740
Sorry for being young.

00:14:52.710 --> 00:14:56.520
I don't know about a date, 
but do you want to stop somewhere?

00:14:56.520 --> 00:14:57.780
Shopping or something?

00:15:29.460 --> 00:15:32.010
Hello again, you two.

00:15:32.010 --> 00:15:33.990
The battle's over,

00:15:33.990 --> 00:15:35.420
so once again...

00:15:35.420 --> 00:15:39.870
I am Awaza Kodama's manager,
Moriyama Hibiki with Echo Productions.

00:15:40.820 --> 00:15:43.050
Um, thanks.

00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:46.060
Isn't her song nice?

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:47.880
Yes, it is.

00:15:49.030 --> 00:15:51.880
I didn't have time to think about 
it when I was fighting, but...

00:15:52.580 --> 00:15:54.330
Um, we're...

00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:56.520
Kodama-chan's not letting it get her down.

00:15:57.140 --> 00:15:58.890
Thanks for coming.

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:00.140
Thanks!

00:16:00.140 --> 00:16:01.930
Today, the front of the station is...

00:16:01.930 --> 00:16:03.900
filled with people, huh?

00:16:04.260 --> 00:16:06.010
What's wrong, Kodama-chan?

00:16:06.010 --> 00:16:08.940
No, I just thought I saw someone I knew.

00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:13.410
Why not come to one of 
Kodama-chan's concerts?

00:16:14.260 --> 00:16:15.600
They were good songs.

00:16:15.600 --> 00:16:17.740
Yes, I think so, too.

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:21.410
Next time I'd like to go to 
hear her sing, not to fight.

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:25.580
I guarantee you her songs will 
echo in your soul, or my name's n—

00:16:26.020 --> 00:16:26.940
President Nabeta!

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:27.900
Excuse me!

00:16:27.900 --> 00:16:29.420
I'll be right back.

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:33.430
My private life is pretty boring actually.

00:16:38.070 --> 00:16:40.310
It really was a nice song.

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:41.000
Yeah.

00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:45.080
It's amazing, huh? Big and huge.

00:16:50.660 --> 00:16:52.620
We just kinda came over here.

00:16:52.620 --> 00:16:54.450
Is there anything you want?

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:58.620
Precious Memories.

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:00.100
Are you sure?

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:03.460
You're right.

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:06.260
Maybe I will try it out.

00:17:06.720 --> 00:17:07.960
Teach me to play.

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:13.100
But if you want to buy cards, 
this isn't the place.

00:17:13.100 --> 00:17:14.470
Want to go back?

00:17:15.340 --> 00:17:17.470
<b>Makihara-sensei</b>

00:17:16.160 --> 00:17:17.470
Makihara-sensei?

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:20.700
Hello. We're in a building 
near the station...

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:22.890
So are you?

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:24.150
An exhibition?

00:17:24.150 --> 00:17:26.280
I didn't know there was one.

00:17:26.280 --> 00:17:28.730
Okay, we'll wait here.

00:17:29.990 --> 00:17:32.970
Makihara-sensei says 
he just happens to be nearby.

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:36.520
The Philosophy of the Human 
Body Labyrinth Exhibition...

00:17:36.520 --> 00:17:37.990
What kind of exhibition is that?

00:17:39.810 --> 00:17:41.130
Hey, Koyori.

00:17:41.520 --> 00:17:43.260
What do you want to do from now on?

00:17:43.260 --> 00:17:45.500
I mean, not just today...

00:17:46.050 --> 00:17:50.220
Well, in the future, when you finally 
let go of each other's hands,

00:17:50.220 --> 00:17:52.710
it will be useful, I bet.

00:17:55.720 --> 00:17:57.950
When Hayate-san said that, I realized...

00:17:57.950 --> 00:18:00.220
Even if it's all we can do to survive now,

00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:02.590
Makihara-sensei's working hard.

00:18:02.590 --> 00:18:05.310
And if we keep winning,

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:07.730
someday we may let go of each other's hands.

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:11.230
What do you want to do then, Koyori?

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:17.210
Stay with you.

00:18:17.210 --> 00:18:18.240
But...

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:20.240
I want to stay with you.

00:18:21.360 --> 00:18:24.350
I see... Even if we don't 
hold each other's hands.

00:18:24.350 --> 00:18:26.250
Yeah. Me, too.

00:18:27.940 --> 00:18:29.250
I want to cook.

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:31.450
That, too?

00:18:31.450 --> 00:18:33.710
And beat you in Precious Memories.

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:37.100
That's not very far in the future.

00:18:37.100 --> 00:18:39.260
Yo! Tazuna-kun! Koyori-kun!

00:18:40.770 --> 00:18:42.340
Sorry! Sorry!

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:45.770
That exhibition was just so good.

00:18:47.400 --> 00:18:51.770
I didn't think it was possible to approach 
the large intestine in such a way.

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:54.110
I bought a pamphlet.

00:18:54.110 --> 00:18:54.770
Want to see?

00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:58.430
No, maybe we could go back.

00:18:58.430 --> 00:19:01.080
All three of us!

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:03.740
I'll pay the fee!

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:04.920
No thanks.

00:19:05.720 --> 00:19:07.250
Precious Memories and a parfait.

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:10.270
No!

00:19:10.270 --> 00:19:13.310
The kids and me just like different things?

00:19:13.310 --> 00:19:15.630
I'm shocked!

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:18.120
It's not like that.

00:19:18.120 --> 00:19:19.260
Just a little?

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:22.260
Want to see the pamphlet, just a little?

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:25.220
I want to go shopping, so we're 
going to shop near the station.

00:19:27.160 --> 00:19:29.270
You're so cold, Tazuna-kun.

00:19:29.920 --> 00:19:33.020
At least get some shumai on your way back.

00:19:56.050 --> 00:19:57.420
That man from before...

00:19:57.680 --> 00:19:58.760
I see.

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:00.710
So that's it?

00:20:01.930 --> 00:20:04.930
<b>The Philosophy of the Human Body
 Labyrinth Exhibition</b>

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:04.930
I thought it was possible.

00:20:05.730 --> 00:20:07.500
I never found out where you went,

00:20:07.500 --> 00:20:09.320
but I didn't think you were dead.

00:20:09.680 --> 00:20:11.380
It's true that you'd be capable of...

00:20:12.470 --> 00:20:14.190
How have you been lately?

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:16.380
Just because it's been a while,

00:20:16.380 --> 00:20:18.250
you can barely even talk to me?

00:20:19.290 --> 00:20:22.200
Makihara-sensei, who is that?

00:20:23.480 --> 00:20:25.200
An old acquaintance.

00:20:26.020 --> 00:20:29.850
We had a deeper relationship, once.

00:20:32.410 --> 00:20:37.070
You're still that man's 
slave, Takatsuki Tazuna?

00:20:37.070 --> 00:20:38.560
I told you.

00:20:38.560 --> 00:20:42.970
Akutagawa Koyori is not Takatsuki Musubu.

00:21:05.540 --> 00:21:08.070
I know Mayumi-kun is there.

00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:11.040
But how did you save her life?

00:21:11.440 --> 00:21:12.540
Don't ask.

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:15.630
Overthinking things is what you do, right?

00:21:15.630 --> 00:21:17.240
But I'll say this.

00:21:17.240 --> 00:21:20.040
It's not a coincidence that I'm here.

00:21:20.450 --> 00:21:23.550
He's a Hand Shaker, too?

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:27.370
I'll tell you everything before I end this.

00:21:27.370 --> 00:21:30.640
About the truth that Makihara won't tell you.

00:23:10.840 --> 00:23:12.620
<i>Koyori and Mayumi.</i>

00:23:12.620 --> 00:23:15.240
<i>A story born from two cocoons.</i>

00:23:15.790 --> 00:23:18.200
<i>The threads weave time back to the past.</i>

00:23:18.990 --> 00:23:21.690
<i>But the threads are so weak and frail...</i>

00:23:22.200 --> 00:23:26.650
<i>What is the reason why the young 
Makihara and Nagaoka cut their bonds?</i>

00:23:27.250 --> 00:23:33.030
<i>Next time on Hand Shakers, 
Episode 11: Cocoon Cocoon.</i>

00:23:33.940 --> 00:23:37.100
<i>Bloodshot eyes staring at sleeping girls...</i>

00:23:37.100 --> 00:23:39.260
<i>Are they filled with madness, or love?</i>
